{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "regret_cluster_selective",
  "intent": "Replace the parent's constant 0.2*regret with a ratio-gated regret using (mean_remaining - nearest_remaining)/mean_remaining as a clustering-intensity detector. In uniform layouts nearest_remaining ≈ mean_remaining, so the regret factor collapses toward 0 and behavior falls back to -distance + 0.25*return_distance (return_aware baseline), suppressing the noisy regret that dominates uniform failure. In clustered/grid layouts nearest_remaining << mean_remaining, the ratio approaches 1 and regret is fully amplified to pick the now-or-later winners earlier. The parent's r/(0.5+nr) nonlinear correction is preserved to further boost candidates with very close remaining neighbors. Hypothesis: this isolates regret to selective pick-now signals where nr/mean is low.",
  "tags": [
    "regret",
    "cluster"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    mr = f['mean_remaining']\n    r = f['regret']\n    cr = (mr - nr) / (mr + 1e-9)\n    denom = 0.5 + nr\n    if denom < 1e-9:\n        denom = 1e-9\n    return -d + 0.25 * rd + 0.2 * r * cr + 0.15 * r / denom",
  "source": "live_llm",
  "parent_id": 17,
  "reference_id": null,
